-- ccc23-assessment.l4 -- sections 672.11 to 672.191 (Assessment Orders) and 672.2 (Assessment Reports) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- FORM. A power ("may") is a decision function: JUST TRUE when the facts bring the case within it; NOTHING where the "if" gate on a grant fails (ruling of 2026-11-12, fork F-GRANT-IF);
-- JUST FALSE where the text closes the gate itself ("only if", "may not ... unless", a flat negative) or where the gate is a "where" (guide ruling (b), fork F-GRANT-WHERE).
-- A bar is named as the bar: JUST TRUE = the bar applies; JUST FALSE = the text's own "unless" exception is met; NOTHING = the text does not speak to the case.
-- A duty is a function whose JUST TRUE means "the duty arises on these facts". Where the text gives a time limit the duty is also a regulative rule, run with #TRACE
-- (a #TRACE outcome cannot be #ASSERTed on the stable binary, so the same duty is a decision function too, and that is what is asserted).
-- Facts are plain BOOLEAN or NUMBER inputs. An answer of another provision is an input named for it.

§ `Section 672.11 -- Assessment order`

-- 672.11: a court having jurisdiction over an accused in respect of an offence may order an assessment of the mental condition of the accused, if it has reasonable grounds to believe
-- that such evidence is necessary to determine (a) fitness, (b) exemption from criminal responsibility under 16(1), (c) disturbed balance of mind (newly-born child), (d) the appropriate disposition after an NCR or unfit verdict,
-- (d.1) whether a high-risk finding should be revoked under 672.84(3), or (e) whether to make a stay order under 672.851 after an unfit verdict.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF
-- src:13335 | 672.11 A court having jurisdiction over an accused in respect of an offence may order an assessment of the mental condition of the accused, if it has reasonable grounds to believe that such evidence is necessary to determine
-- src:13336 | (a) whether the accused is unfit to stand trial;
-- src:13337 | (b) whether the accused was, at the time of the commission of the alleged offence, suffering from a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1);
-- src:13338 | (c) whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence, where the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child;
-- src:13339 | (d) the appropriate disposition to be made, where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused;
-- src:13340 | (d.1) whether a finding that the accused is a high-risk accused should be revoked under subsection 672.84(3); or
-- src:13341 | (e) whether an order should be made under section 672.851 for a stay of proceedings, where a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered against the accused.
@ref s 672.11; s 672.11(a); s 672.11(b); s 672.11(c); s 672.11(d); s 672.11(d.1); s 672.11(e) (src:13335-13341)
GIVEN `the court has jurisdiction over the accused in respect of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the accused was, at the time of the alleged offence, suffering from a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of the alleged offence` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
      `the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine the appropriate disposition` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
      `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether a finding that the accused is a high-risk accused should be revoked under subsection 672.84(3)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d.1)
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether an order should be made under section 672.851 for a stay of proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)
      `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered against the accused` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.11 the court may order an assessment of the mental condition of the accused` MEANS
    IF     `the court has jurisdiction over the accused in respect of an offence`
       AND (    `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial`
             OR `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the accused was, at the time of the alleged offence, suffering from a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)`
             OR (    `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of the alleged offence`
                 AND `the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child`)
             OR (    `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine the appropriate disposition`
                 AND `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial has been rendered in respect of the accused`)
             OR `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether a finding that the accused is a high-risk accused should be revoked under subsection 672.84(3)`
             OR (    `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether an order should be made under section 672.851 for a stay of proceedings`
                 AND `a verdict of unfit to stand trial has been rendered against the accused`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it has reasonable grounds to believe that such evidence is necessary to determine"

§ `Section 672.12 -- Where court may order assessment`

-- 672.12(2): where the prosecutor applies for an assessment to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial for a summary-conviction offence, the court may ONLY order it if
-- (a) the accused raised the issue of fitness, or (b) the prosecutor satisfies the court that there are reasonable grounds to doubt fitness.
-- src:13344 | Limitation on prosecutor’s application for assessment of fitness
-- src:13345 | (2) Where the prosecutor applies for an assessment in order to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial for an offence that is prosecuted by way of summary conviction, the court may only order the assessment if
-- src:13346 | (a) the accused raised the issue of fitness; or
-- src:13347 | (b) the prosecutor satisfies the court that there are reasonable grounds to doubt that the accused is fit to stand trial.
@ref s 672.12(2); s 672.12(2)(a); s 672.12(2)(b) (src:13344-13347)
GIVEN `the prosecutor applies for an assessment to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial for an offence prosecuted by way of summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused raised the issue of fitness` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the prosecutor satisfies the court that there are reasonable grounds to doubt that the accused is fit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.12(2) the court may order the assessment on the prosecutor’s application about fitness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the prosecutor applies for an assessment to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial for an offence prosecuted by way of summary conviction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Where the prosecutor applies for an assessment in order to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial for an offence that is prosecuted by way of summary conviction"
        IF `the accused raised the issue of fitness` OR `the prosecutor satisfies the court that there are reasonable grounds to doubt that the accused is fit to stand trial` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court may only order the assessment if"

-- 672.12(3): where the prosecutor applies for an assessment to determine whether the accused was suffering from a mental disorder at the time of the offence so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility,
-- the court may ONLY order it if (a) the accused puts his or her mental capacity for criminal intent into issue, or (b) the prosecutor satisfies the court that there are reasonable grounds to doubt criminal responsibility.
-- src:13348 | Limitation on prosecutor’s application for assessment
-- src:13349 | (3) Where the prosecutor applies for an assessment in order to determine whether the accused was suffering from a mental disorder at the time of the offence so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility, the court may only order the assessment if
-- src:13350 | (a) the accused puts his or her mental capacity for criminal intent into issue; or
-- src:13351 | (b) the prosecutor satisfies the court that there are reasonable grounds to doubt that the accused is criminally responsible for the alleged offence, on account of mental disorder.
@ref s 672.12(3); s 672.12(3)(a); s 672.12(3)(b) (src:13348-13351)
GIVEN `the prosecutor applies for an assessment to determine whether the accused was suffering from a mental disorder at the time of the offence so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused puts his or her mental capacity for criminal intent into issue` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the prosecutor satisfies the court that there are reasonable grounds to doubt that the accused is criminally responsible for the alleged offence, on account of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.12(3) the court may order the assessment on the prosecutor’s application about criminal responsibility` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the prosecutor applies for an assessment to determine whether the accused was suffering from a mental disorder at the time of the offence so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Where the prosecutor applies for an assessment in order to determine whether the accused was suffering from a mental disorder"
        IF `the accused puts his or her mental capacity for criminal intent into issue` OR `the prosecutor satisfies the court that there are reasonable grounds to doubt that the accused is criminally responsible for the alleged offence, on account of mental disorder` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court may only order the assessment if"

-- 672.12(1): the court may make an assessment order at any stage of proceedings against the accused, of its own motion, on application of the accused or, subject to subsections (2) and (3), on application of the prosecutor.
-- The two inputs `by s 672.12(2)` and `by s 672.12(3)` are the answers of the two functions above for the prosecutor's application (NOTHING: the subsection does not speak to that application).
