§ `Section 672.121 -- Review Board may order assessment`

-- 672.121: the Review Board that has jurisdiction over an accused found NCR or unfit may order an assessment of its own motion or on application of the prosecutor or the accused, if it has reasonable grounds to believe
-- that such evidence is necessary to (a) make a recommendation under 672.851(1); (b) make a disposition under 672.54 where (i) no assessment report is available, (ii) none has been conducted in the last twelve months, or (iii) the accused has been transferred
-- from another province under 672.86; or (c) determine whether to refer a high-risk finding to the court for review under 672.84(1).
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF
-- src:13353 | 672.121 The Review Board that has jurisdiction over an accused found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial may order an assessment of the mental condition of the accused of its own motion or on application of the prosecutor or the accused, if it has reasonable grounds to believe that such evidence is necessary to
-- src:13354 | (a) make a recommendation to the court under subsection 672.851(1);
-- src:13355 | (b) make a disposition under section 672.54 in one of the following circumstances:
-- src:13356 | (i) no assessment report on the mental condition of the accused is available,
-- src:13357 | (ii) no assessment of the mental condition of the accused has been conducted in the last twelve months, or
-- src:13358 | (iii) the accused has been transferred from another province under section 672.86; or
-- src:13359 | (c) determine whether to refer to the court for review under subsection 672.84(1) a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused.
@ref s 672.121; s 672.121(a); s 672.121(b); s 672.121(b)(i); s 672.121(b)(ii); s 672.121(b)(iii); s 672.121(c) (src:13353-13359)
GIVEN `the Review Board has jurisdiction over an accused found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Review Board acts of its own motion or on application of the prosecutor or the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to make a recommendation to the court under subsection 672.851(1)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to make a disposition under section 672.54` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `no assessment report on the mental condition of the accused is available` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(i)
      `no assessment of the mental condition of the accused has been conducted in the last twelve months` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(ii)
      `the accused has been transferred from another province under section 672.86` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)(iii)
      `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether to refer to the court for review under subsection 672.84(1) a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.121 the Review Board may order an assessment of the mental condition of the accused` MEANS
    IF     `the Review Board has jurisdiction over an accused found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial`
       AND `the Review Board acts of its own motion or on application of the prosecutor or the accused`
       AND (    `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to make a recommendation to the court under subsection 672.851(1)`
             OR (    `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to make a disposition under section 672.54`
                 AND (    `no assessment report on the mental condition of the accused is available`
                       OR `no assessment of the mental condition of the accused has been conducted in the last twelve months`
                       OR `the accused has been transferred from another province under section 672.86`))
             OR `reasonable grounds to believe that an assessment is necessary to determine whether to refer to the court for review under subsection 672.84(1) a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it has reasonable grounds to believe that such evidence is necessary to"

§ `Section 672.13 -- Contents of assessment order`

-- 672.13(1): an assessment order must specify (a) the service or person who is to make the assessment, or the hospital where it is to be made; (b) whether the accused is to be detained in custody while the order is in force; and
-- (c) the period that the order is to be in force, including the time for the accused to travel to and from the place of assessment. A bare "must": JUST FALSE where a limb is missing (fork F-MUST-BARE).
-- fork: F-MUST-BARE
-- src:13361 | 672.13 (1) An assessment order must specify
-- src:13362 | (a) the service that or the person who is to make the assessment, or the hospital where it is to be made;
-- src:13363 | (b) whether the accused is to be detained in custody while the order is in force; and
-- src:13364 | (c) the period that the order is to be in force, including the time required for the assessment and for the accused to travel to and from the place where the assessment is to be made.
@ref s 672.13(1); s 672.13(1)(a); s 672.13(1)(b); s 672.13(1)(c) (src:13361-13364)
GIVEN `it specifies the service that or the person who is to make the assessment, or the hospital where it is to be made` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `it specifies whether the accused is to be detained in custody while the order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `it specifies the period that the order is to be in force, including the time required for the assessment and for the accused to travel to and from the place where the assessment is to be made` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.13(1) the assessment order has the contents the section requires` MEANS
    IF     `it specifies the service that or the person who is to make the assessment, or the hospital where it is to be made`
       AND `it specifies whether the accused is to be detained in custody while the order is in force`
       AND `it specifies the period that the order is to be in force, including the time required for the assessment and for the accused to travel to and from the place where the assessment is to be made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An assessment order must specify"

-- 672.13(2): an assessment order may be in Form 48 or 48.1.
-- src:13366 | (2) An assessment order may be in Form 48 or 48.1.
@ref s 672.13(2) (src:13366)
GIVEN `the order is in Form 48` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is in Form 48.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.13(2) the assessment order is in a form the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the order is in Form 48` OR `the order is in Form 48.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "An assessment order may be in Form 48 or 48.1"

§ `Section 672.14 -- Period of an assessment order`

-- 672.14(1): an assessment order shall not be in force for more than thirty days. A flat negative: over thirty is JUST FALSE.
-- src:13368 | 672.14 (1) An assessment order shall not be in force for more than thirty days.
@ref s 672.14(1) (src:13368)
GIVEN `the number of days the order is to be in force` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.14(1) the assessment order is within the general limit of thirty days` MEANS
    IF `the number of days the order is to be in force` AT MOST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An assessment order shall not be in force for more than thirty days"

-- 672.14(2): no assessment order to determine fitness shall be in force for more than five days, excluding holidays and the time to travel to and from the place of assessment, unless the accused and the prosecutor agree to a longer period not exceeding thirty days.
-- The days counted here are the days the text counts (holidays and travel time excluded).
-- src:13370 | (2) No assessment order to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial shall be in force for more than five days, excluding holidays and the time required for the accused to travel to and from the place where the assessment is to be made, unless the accused and the prosecutor agree to a longer period not exceeding thirty days.
@ref s 672.14(2) (src:13370)
GIVEN `the order is to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days the order is to be in force, excluding holidays and the time required to travel` IS A NUMBER
      `the accused and the prosecutor agree to a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.14(2) the fitness assessment order is within the limit of five days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the order is to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "No assessment order to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial"
        IF `the number of days the order is to be in force, excluding holidays and the time required to travel` AT MOST 5 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the accused and the prosecutor agree to a longer period` AND `the number of days the order is to be in force, excluding holidays and the time required to travel` AT MOST 30 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be in force for more than five days"

-- 672.14(3): despite (1) and (2), a court or Review Board may make an assessment order that remains in force for sixty days if it is satisfied that compelling circumstances exist that warrant it.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF
-- src:13372 | (3) Despite subsections (1) and (2), a court or Review Board may make an assessment order that remains in force for sixty days if the court or Review Board is satisfied that compelling circumstances exist that warrant it.
@ref s 672.14(3) (src:13372)
GIVEN `the court or Review Board is satisfied that compelling circumstances exist that warrant it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days the order is to be in force` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.14(3) the court or Review Board may make an assessment order that remains in force for sixty days` MEANS
    IF `the court or Review Board is satisfied that compelling circumstances exist that warrant it` AND `the number of days the order is to be in force` AT MOST 60
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court or Review Board is satisfied that compelling circumstances exist that warrant it"

-- The three subsections together: the longest an assessment order may be in force, in days. Compelling circumstances give sixty; otherwise a fitness order gives five (excluding holidays and travel) unless the accused and the prosecutor agree, when it is thirty;
-- every other order is thirty. The composition is the text's own order of precedence ("Despite subsections (1) and (2)").
-- src:13368 | 672.14 (1) An assessment order shall not be in force for more than thirty days.
-- src:13369 | Exception in fitness cases
-- src:13370 | (2) No assessment order to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial shall be in force for more than five days, excluding holidays and the time required for the accused to travel to and from the place where the assessment is to be made, unless the accused and the prosecutor agree to a longer period not exceeding thirty days.
-- src:13371 | Exception for compelling circumstances
-- src:13372 | (3) Despite subsections (1) and (2), a court or Review Board may make an assessment order that remains in force for sixty days if the court or Review Board is satisfied that compelling circumstances exist that warrant it.
@ref s 672.14(1); s 672.14(2); s 672.14(3) (src:13368-13372)
GIVEN `compelling circumstances that warrant it exist, and the court or Review Board is satisfied of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused and the prosecutor agree to a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 672.14 the longest period the assessment order may be in force, in days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `compelling circumstances that warrant it exist, and the court or Review Board is satisfied of it` THEN 60
        IF `the order is to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` AND `the accused and the prosecutor agree to a longer period` THEN 30
        IF `the order is to determine whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` THEN 5   -- five days excluding holidays and travel time
        OTHERWISE 30

§ `Section 672.15 -- Extension`

-- 672.15(2): no extension of an assessment order shall exceed thirty days, and the period of the initial order together with all extensions shall not exceed sixty days.
-- src:13376 | (2) No extension of an assessment order shall exceed thirty days, and the period of the initial order together with all extensions shall not exceed sixty days.
@ref s 672.15(2) (src:13376)
GIVEN `the days of the extension` IS A NUMBER
      `the days of the initial order together with all extensions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.15(2) the extension is within the maximum` MEANS
    IF `the days of the extension` AT MOST 30 AND `the days of the initial order together with all extensions` AT MOST 60
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No extension of an assessment order shall exceed thirty days"

-- 672.15(1): subject to (2), a court or Review Board may extend an assessment order, of its own motion or on the application of the accused or the prosecutor made during or at the end of the period during which the order is in force,
-- for any further period that is required, in its opinion, to complete the assessment.
