@ref s 672.15(1) (src:13374)
GIVEN `the court or Review Board acts of its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused or the prosecutor applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made during or at the end of the period during which the order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the further period is required, in its opinion, to complete the assessment of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extension is within the maximum, by s 672.15(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.15(1) the court or Review Board may extend the assessment order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the further period is required, in its opinion, to complete the assessment of the accused` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any further period that is required, in its opinion, to complete the assessment of the accused"
        IF `the extension is within the maximum, by s 672.15(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (2)"
        IF `the court or Review Board acts of its own motion` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the accused or the prosecutor applies` AND `the application is made during or at the end of the period during which the order is in force` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the accused or the prosecutor applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "made during or at the end of the period during which the order is in force"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "of its own motion or on the application of the accused or the prosecutor"

§ `Section 672.16 -- Presumption against custody`

-- 672.16(1): subject to (3), an accused shall not be detained in custody under an assessment order of a court unless (a) the court is satisfied on the evidence that custody is necessary to assess the accused, or on the evidence of a
-- medical practitioner that custody is desirable and the accused consents; (b) custody is required in respect of any other matter or by virtue of any other provision of this Act; or (c) the prosecutor, having been given a reasonable opportunity,
-- shows that detention is justified on either of the grounds in subsection 515(10). Named as the bar: JUST TRUE = the bar applies; JUST FALSE = one of (a) to (c) is met.
-- fork: F-SUBJECT
-- src:13378 | 672.16 (1) Subject to subsection (3), an accused shall not be detained in custody under an assessment order of a court unless
-- src:13379 | (a) the court is satisfied that on the evidence custody is necessary to assess the accused, or that on the evidence of a medical practitioner custody is desirable to assess the accused and the accused consents to custody;
-- src:13380 | (b) custody of the accused is required in respect of any other matter or by virtue of any other provision of this Act; or
-- src:13381 | (c) the prosecutor, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shows that detention of the accused in custody is justified on either of the grounds set out in subsection 515(10).
@ref s 672.16(1); s 672.16(1)(a); s 672.16(1)(b); s 672.16(1)(c) (src:13378-13381)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied on the evidence that custody is necessary to assess the accused` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `on the evidence of a medical practitioner custody is desirable to assess the accused` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the accused consents to custody` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `custody of the accused is required in respect of any other matter or by virtue of any other provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `the prosecutor, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shows that detention is justified on either of the grounds set out in subsection 515(10)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.16(1) the court is barred from detaining the accused in custody under the assessment order` MEANS
    IF     `the court is satisfied on the evidence that custody is necessary to assess the accused`
        OR (`on the evidence of a medical practitioner custody is desirable to assess the accused` AND `the accused consents to custody`)
        OR `custody of the accused is required in respect of any other matter or by virtue of any other provision of this Act`
        OR `the prosecutor, having been given a reasonable opportunity to do so, shows that detention is justified on either of the grounds set out in subsection 515(10)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be detained in custody under an assessment order of a court unless"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- 672.16(1.1): if the Review Board makes an order for an assessment under 672.121, the accused shall not be detained in custody under the order unless (a) the accused is currently subject to a disposition under 672.54(c);
-- (b) the Review Board is satisfied on the evidence that custody is necessary to assess the accused, or on the evidence of a medical practitioner that custody is desirable and the accused consents; or (c) custody is required in respect of any other matter or by any other provision of this Act.
