§ `Sections 672.17 to 672.19 -- Bail, variation, treatment`

-- 672.17: during the period that an assessment order made by a court in respect of an accused charged with an offence is in force, no order for the interim release or detention of the accused may be made by virtue of Part XVI or section 679 in respect of that offence or an included offence.
-- src:13394 | 672.17 During the period that an assessment order made by a court in respect of an accused charged with an offence is in force, no order for the interim release or detention of the accused may be made by virtue of Part XVI or section 679 in respect of that offence or an included offence.
@ref s 672.17 (src:13394)
GIVEN `an assessment order made by a court is in force in respect of the accused charged with an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order sought is for the interim release or detention of the accused in respect of that offence or an included offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order would be made by virtue of Part XVI or section 679` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.17 the section bars an order for the interim release or detention of the accused` MEANS
    IF     `an assessment order made by a court is in force in respect of the accused charged with an offence`
       AND `the order sought is for the interim release or detention of the accused in respect of that offence or an included offence`
       AND `the order would be made by virtue of Part XVI or section 679`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "During the period that an assessment order made by a court in respect of an accused charged with an offence is in force"

-- 672.18: where at any time while an assessment order made by a court is in force the prosecutor or an accused shows cause, the court may vary the terms of the order respecting the interim release or detention of the accused in such manner as it considers appropriate.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13396 | 672.18 Where at any time while an assessment order made by a court is in force the prosecutor or an accused shows cause, the court may vary the terms of the order respecting the interim release or detention of the accused in such manner as it considers appropriate in the circumstances.
@ref s 672.18 (src:13396)
GIVEN `an assessment order made by a court is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor or an accused shows cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.18 the court may vary the terms of the assessment order respecting interim release or detention` MEANS
    IF `an assessment order made by a court is in force` AND `the prosecutor or an accused shows cause`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where at any time while an assessment order made by a court is in force the prosecutor or an accused shows cause"

-- 672.19: no assessment order may direct that psychiatric or any other treatment of the accused be carried out, or direct the accused to submit to such treatment.
-- src:13398 | 672.19 No assessment order may direct that psychiatric or any other treatment of the accused be carried out, or direct the accused to submit to such treatment.
@ref s 672.19 (src:13398)
GIVEN `the term directs that psychiatric or any other treatment of the accused be carried out, or directs the accused to submit to such treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.19 the section bars an assessment order from directing treatment` MEANS
    IF `the term directs that psychiatric or any other treatment of the accused be carried out, or directs the accused to submit to such treatment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "No assessment order may direct that psychiatric or any other treatment of the accused be carried out"

§ `Section 672.191 -- When assessment completed`

-- 672.191: an accused in respect of whom an assessment order is made shall appear before the court or Review Board that made the order as soon as practicable after the assessment is completed and not later than the last day of the period that the order is to be in force.
-- As a regulative rule the accused's duty is run for the days up to the last day; "as soon as practicable" has no number and is not modelled in the rule (the decision function takes it as a plain fact).
-- src:13400 | 672.191 An accused in respect of whom an assessment order is made shall appear before the court or Review Board that made the order as soon as practicable after the assessment is completed and not later than the last day of the period that the order is to be in force.
@ref s 672.191 (src:13400)
DECLARE `s 672.191 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 672.191 appear before the court or Review Board that made the order`

GIVEN `days from the start of the assessment order to the last day of the period that the order is to be in force` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 672.191 act`
`s 672.191 the accused must appear after the assessment is completed` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 672.191 appear before the court or Review Board that made the order`
    WITHIN `days from the start of the assessment order to the last day of the period that the order is to be in force`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "the accused did not appear before the court or Review Board by the last day of the period that the assessment order was to be in force"

-- The same duty as a decision function over dates: JUST TRUE if the accused appeared not later than the last day and as soon as practicable; JUST FALSE otherwise (a bare "shall": fork F-MUST-BARE).
-- fork: F-MUST-BARE
@ref s 672.191 (src:13400)
GIVEN `the day the assessment order begins` IS A DATE
      `the number of days the order is to be in force` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the accused appears before the court or Review Board that made the order` IS A DATE
      `the accused appeared as soon as practicable after the assessment was completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.191 the accused has appeared as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the accused appeared as soon as practicable after the assessment was completed` AND `the day the accused appears before the court or Review Board that made the order` AT MOST (`the day the assessment order begins` PLUS `the number of days the order is to be in force`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall appear before the court or Review Board that made the order as soon as practicable after the assessment is completed and not later than the last day of the period"

§ `Section 672.2 -- Assessment reports`

-- 672.2(1): an assessment order may require the person who makes the assessment to submit in writing an assessment report on the mental condition of the accused.
-- src:13404 | 672.2 (1) An assessment order may require the person who makes the assessment to submit in writing an assessment report on the mental condition of the accused.
