GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.2(3) the court must send a copy of the report to the Review Board without delay` MEANS
    IF `a report has been filed with the court pursuant to subsection 672.2(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any report filed with it pursuant to subsection (2)"

-- 672.2(4): subject to subsection 672.51(3), copies of any report filed with a court or Review Board under (2) shall be provided without delay to the prosecutor, the accused and any counsel representing the accused.
-- fork: F-SUBJECT, F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13410 | (4) Subject to subsection 672.51(3), copies of any report filed with a court or Review Board under subsection (2) shall be provided without delay to the prosecutor, the accused and any counsel representing the accused.
@ref s 672.2(4) (src:13410)
GIVEN `a report has been filed with a court or Review Board under subsection 672.2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 672.51(3) requires the court or Review Board to withhold the information from the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.2(4) the report must be provided to the accused and counsel without delay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a report has been filed with a court or Review Board under subsection 672.2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "copies of any report filed with a court or Review Board under subsection (2)"
        IF `subsection 672.51(3) requires the court or Review Board to withhold the information from the accused` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection 672.51(3)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 672.21 -- Protected statements`

-- 672.21(1): protected statement means a statement made by the accused during the course and for the purposes of an assessment or treatment directed by a disposition, to the person specified in the assessment order or the disposition, or to anyone acting under that person's direction.
-- src:13414 | 672.21 (1) In this section, protected statement means a statement made by the accused during the course and for the purposes of an assessment or treatment directed by a disposition, to the person specified in the assessment order or the disposition, or to anyone acting under that person’s direction.
@ref s 672.21(1); s 672.21(1)"protected statement" (src:13414)
GIVEN `it is a statement made by the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made during the course and for the purposes of an assessment or treatment directed by a disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made to the person specified in the assessment order or the disposition, or to anyone acting under that person’s direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.21(1) protected statement` MEANS
    IF `it is a statement made by the accused` AND `it is made during the course and for the purposes of an assessment or treatment directed by a disposition` AND `it is made to the person specified in the assessment order or the disposition, or to anyone acting under that person’s direction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "protected statement means a statement made by the accused during the course and for the purposes of an assessment or treatment directed by a disposition"

-- 672.21(3): notwithstanding (2), evidence of a protected statement is admissible for the purpose of (a) determining whether the accused is unfit to stand trial; (b) making a disposition or placement decision;
-- (c) determining under section 672.84 whether to refer or revoke a high-risk finding; (d) determining whether the balance of the mind was disturbed (a female person charged re the death of her newly-born child); (e) determining whether the accused was suffering from
-- automatism or a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility, if the accused puts mental capacity for criminal intent into issue, or if the prosecutor raises the issue after verdict; (f) challenging the credibility of an accused where the testimony is inconsistent
-- in a material particular with a protected statement made previously; (g) establishing the perjury of an accused who is charged with perjury in respect of a statement made in any proceeding. The list is not closed by "only": a purpose not listed is NOTHING.
-- src:13418 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (2), evidence of a protected statement is admissible for the purpose of
-- src:13419 | (a) determining whether the accused is unfit to stand trial;
-- src:13420 | (b) making a disposition or placement decision respecting the accused;
-- src:13421 | (c) determining, under section 672.84, whether to refer to the court for review a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused or whether to revoke such a finding;
-- src:13422 | (d) determining whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence, where the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child;
-- src:13423 | (e) determining whether the accused was, at the time of the commission of an alleged offence, suffering from automatism or a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1), if the accused puts his or her mental capacity for criminal intent into issue, or if the prosecutor raises the issue after verdict;
-- src:13424 | (f) challenging the credibility of an accused in any proceeding where the testimony of the accused is inconsistent in a material particular with a protected statement that the accused made previously; or
-- src:13425 | (g) establishing the perjury of an accused who is charged with perjury in respect of a statement made in any proceeding.
@ref s 672.21(3); s 672.21(3)(a); s 672.21(3)(b); s 672.21(3)(c); s 672.21(3)(d); s 672.21(3)(e); s 672.21(3)(f); s 672.21(3)(g) (src:13418-13425)
GIVEN `the purpose is determining whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the purpose is making a disposition or placement decision respecting the accused` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `the purpose is determining, under section 672.84, whether to refer to the court for review a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused or whether to revoke such a finding` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
      `the purpose is determining whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence, and the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
      `the purpose is determining whether the accused was, at the time of the commission of an alleged offence, suffering from automatism or a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)
      `the accused puts his or her mental capacity for criminal intent into issue, or the prosecutor raises the issue after verdict` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)
      `the purpose is challenging the credibility of an accused in a proceeding where the testimony of the accused is inconsistent in a material particular with a protected statement that the accused made previously` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (f)
      `the purpose is establishing the perjury of an accused who is charged with perjury in respect of a statement made in any proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (g)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.21(3) evidence of a protected statement is admissible for the purpose` MEANS
    IF     `the purpose is determining whether the accused is unfit to stand trial`
        OR `the purpose is making a disposition or placement decision respecting the accused`
        OR `the purpose is determining, under section 672.84, whether to refer to the court for review a finding that an accused is a high-risk accused or whether to revoke such a finding`
        OR `the purpose is determining whether the balance of the mind of the accused was disturbed at the time of commission of the alleged offence, and the accused is a female person charged with an offence arising out of the death of her newly-born child`
        OR (`the purpose is determining whether the accused was, at the time of the commission of an alleged offence, suffering from automatism or a mental disorder so as to be exempt from criminal responsibility by virtue of subsection 16(1)` AND `the accused puts his or her mental capacity for criminal intent into issue, or the prosecutor raises the issue after verdict`)
        OR `the purpose is challenging the credibility of an accused in a proceeding where the testimony of the accused is inconsistent in a material particular with a protected statement that the accused made previously`
        OR `the purpose is establishing the perjury of an accused who is charged with perjury in respect of a statement made in any proceeding`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "evidence of a protected statement is admissible for the purpose of"

-- 672.21(2): no protected statement or reference to a protected statement made by an accused is admissible in evidence, without the consent of the accused, in any proceeding before a court, tribunal, body or person
-- with jurisdiction to compel the production of evidence. Named as the bar: JUST TRUE = the bar applies. Subsection (3) is the text's own "Notwithstanding": when it makes the evidence admissible the bar does not apply (JUST FALSE).
-- fork: F-WITHOUT-CONSENT
-- src:13416 | (2) No protected statement or reference to a protected statement made by an accused is admissible in evidence, without the consent of the accused, in any proceeding before a court, tribunal, body or person with jurisdiction to compel the production of evidence.
@ref s 672.21(2) (src:13416)
GIVEN `it is a protected statement, or a reference to a protected statement, made by an accused, by s 672.21(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is before a court, tribunal, body or person with jurisdiction to compel the production of evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is admissible for the purpose, by s 672.21(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.21(2) the section bars the protected statement from being admitted in evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a protected statement, or a reference to a protected statement, made by an accused, by s 672.21(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No protected statement or reference to a protected statement made by an accused"
        IF `it is a protected statement, or a reference to a protected statement, made by an accused, by s 672.21(1)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "protected statement"
        IF `the evidence is admissible for the purpose, by s 672.21(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notwithstanding subsection (2), evidence of a protected statement is admissible for the purpose of"
        IF `the accused consents` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of the accused"
        IF NOT `the proceeding is before a court, tribunal, body or person with jurisdiction to compel the production of evidence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any proceeding before a court, tribunal, body or person with jurisdiction to compel the production of evidence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
